<pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Iabb075a48d8d1e3e1811afeaad5ab47e7846c972" commit="356e32d962f1066dcd5c6695beb614a56c94cbbb" commit_message="UPSTREAM: timestamp: Bump CBMEM timestamp count, make full use of pre-RAM regions  Since we're reaching the timestamp limit on certain platforms (both for the pre-RAM cache and the final CBMEM region), this patch increases the amount of space for both. In the pre-RAM case, it achieves this by always utilizing the full size of the TIMESTAMP() region allocated in memlayout.ld, rather than arbitrarily limiting it to some constant.  BRANCH=None BUG=None TEST=Booted Oak and confirmed that I can once again see all pre-RAM timestamps after picking in the LZ4 patch series.  Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/13651 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 69d20c45ecd8d224f1e9cf785f4fa441feb6e0a3) Change-Id: Iabb075a48d8d1e3e1811afeaad5ab47e7846c972 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328541 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328541" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/41/328541/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I557a4b263018511d17baa4177963130a97ea310a" commit="94e9aad2ae1b40c50d0ab886fca2f17834f85c24" commit_message="UPSTREAM: timestamp: Remove HAS_PRECBMEM_TIMESTAMP_REGION Kconfig  This patch generalizes the approach previously used for ARM32 TTB_SUBTABLES to &quot;auto-detect&quot; whether a certain region was defined in memlayout.ld. This allows us to get rid of the explicit Kconfig for the TIMESTAMP region, reducing configuration redundancy and avoiding confusion when setting up future boards.  (Removing armv4/bootblock_simple.c because it references this Kconfig and it is a dead file that I just forgot to remove in CL:12076.)  BRANCH=None BUG=None TEST=Booted Oak and confirmed that all pre-RAM timestamps are still there. Built Nyan and Falco.  Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/13652 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 8c09377deab1b5a5120889bb6c689ad460381c29) Change-Id: I557a4b263018511d17baa4177963130a97ea310a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328542 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328542" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/42/328542/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0cde3c0996191ac59dc5c5f6a0b4907b53c0dff8" commit="0d7b09320461d2fba843dd0f407bf5bc52c91125" commit_message="overlord: Darwin/XNU compatibility  Go version: Separate system related utils to sysutils_{GOOS}.go to provide operating system compatibility for Linux and MacOS X.  Python version: Use platform.system() to switch between Linux and Darwin implementations.  BUG=chromium:585733 TEST=`go/src/overlord/test/overlord_e2e_unittest.py`  Change-Id: I0cde3c0996191ac59dc5c5f6a0b4907b53c0dff8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327029 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="327029" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="13" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/29/327029/13" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I90dbecbde5d2fde9ac973c99a1ecbe3958d8ad96" commit="a0559d1b3ca331bb904d9a663d8949d15951366a" commit_message="overlord: fix all warning generated by running golint  The previous commit does not run golint on submission. The commit fix all the warnings generated by golint.  BUG=none TEST=`go/src/overlord/test/overlord_e2e_unittest.py`  Change-Id: I90dbecbde5d2fde9ac973c99a1ecbe3958d8ad96 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327122 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="327122" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/22/327122/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I97afbf7a6919309514bfa0e0446b54b6c85ab819" commit="ff036ec38777c16eb542da3e1b9923b78fe461e6" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Add reconnect mechanism to HFP/HSP  A2DP has reconnect mechanism implemented in plugin/policy.c, at connection failure with err code -EAGAIN, a timer will be scheduled to initiate connection in 2 seconds. A confusing scenario is observed occasionally that user got only A2DP when a BT headset is connected, but not HFP or HSP. When it happens, user is unable to use bidrectional audio, and with headset disconnected and then reconnected, both A2DP and HFP/HSP work fine.  This change adds similar reconnect mechanism for HFP/HSP, so that Chrome OS users can have more consistent experience on BT audio.  BUG=chromium:527575 TEST=Connect BT headset, disconnect and reconnect. Verify this audio device cab be used for A2DP and HFP/HSP.  Change-Id: I97afbf7a6919309514bfa0e0446b54b6c85ab819 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304441 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="304441" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/bluez" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/bluez" ref="refs/changes/41/304441/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7b86b587d0c0855a797798bda0e4b16bbdb27421" commit="b08e6f350f01f2bc53cb68154ea92fdc0131dfe4" commit_message="CRAS: alsa - Don't use card index to calculate stable_id  Card index is not guaranteed consistent each time system boots. When an USB headset is plugged at systen reboot, there are two sound cards to be detected. So that the internal sound card could have index '0' or '1', while the USB headset has index '1' or '0'.  BUG=None TEST=Plug USB headset and reboots several times and monitor the stable_id of each nodes.  Change-Id: I7b86b587d0c0855a797798bda0e4b16bbdb27421 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328561 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328561" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/61/328561/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I97c3615ddfd00b8caedf90e8161bb21917f1bc6a" commit="da0b17b6963f39e34cc3a426ec8c1a60603e800a" commit_message="init: Revise startup flow.  To support running factory for different environments, (for instance, only running Whale and not Goofy), we want to make the init more flexible for controlling each rules executed.  This change has introduced &quot;enable-&quot; and &quot;disable-&quot; tags so we can merge Whale and Goofy into same startup daemon folder, which also makes building packages easier. The run.d is replaced by main.d because we don't need to create run_NAME tags anymore (the new tags can now fully control the default state of each rule).  factory/init/startup is also enhanced to support one argument so that factory-init.conf and factory.conf may share same command by running factory/init/startup with different modes, which helps to prevent hard-coding &quot;goofy_control&quot; in factory.conf (so we can start different services that are not Goofy).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:30239 TEST=make test; started Goofy on Chromebook.  Change-Id: I97c3615ddfd00b8caedf90e8161bb21917f1bc6a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328132 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328132" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/32/328132/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7940.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>